  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Counter from the middle third",
  "description": "Played on a full pitch split into thirds. Blue is a full team. Red has a goalkeeper, a back line and a midfield – no forwards. Blue's midfield and back line stand in the middle third, and blue's forwards stand in the last third against red's back line and goalkeeper.\n\nRed's goalkeeper starts by playing to their midfield, who must keep the ball in the middle third. Blue must win the ball there and counter into the last third as quickly as possible. Red's midfielders may only be in the middle third. If red's back line wins the ball they play it back up to the midfield.\n\nProgression: red's midfielders may leave the middle third and run back when the ball is played into their own third – so blue must counter even faster. The diagram shows fewer players and is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Press together in the middle so the red player is forced into a difficult pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The first look after winning the ball is forward – can it go straight to a forward?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Forwards: make yourselves available in behind before the ball is won."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Support from midfield – the counter needs more than the forwards."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp5",
      "text": "Red back line: drop off and give yourselves time when the counter comes."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
